Spec: LibStorageClassEnrich

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Turn a cluster's raw StorageClass list into the deployment-time storage vocabulary: enrich
    each class from a curated CSI-driver capability/access-mode catalog, expand raw-block
    drivers into twin Block+Filesystem entries, and reduce the list to one named-preference map
    (@class_enrich's output feeds `cluster.storage_classes` and `cluster.prefered_storage`) so
    templates and @storage_class_selector choose classes by role key instead of reading cluster
    annotations themselves.

Exposes:
  @classes_enrich(scs) — the main entry (importers reach it as `sce::classes_enrich(...)` via
    `import "storage_class_enrich" as sce` in ./build_context.rhai). Returns the enriched Array.
  @get_prefered_sc(scs) — second entry; consumes enriched classes, returns the 9-slot
    `#{...}` preference map of class-name Strings or unit.
  @pick_sc(scs) — "default else first" name selector; also called back into @get_prefered_sc.
  @get_known_class() — the 12-entry driver catalog (rebuilt fresh on every call, no cache;
    @classes_enrich rebuilds it once per enrichment loop iteration).
  @get_default_access_modes_from_all(all) — precedence collapse `ReadWriteMany` >
    `ReadWriteOnce` > passthrough.

Accepts:
  @classes_enrich — Array of StorageClass maps. Required per entry: @provisioner (@String —
    only @contains on it is read). All other keys pass through untouched; @volumeMode,
    `capabilities`, @allAccessModes, @accessModes are SET (overwritten) on the returned copies.
  @get_prefered_sc — enriched entries: reads @volumeMode, @accessModes (array @String
    equality match), @provisioner, @is_default, and @name (via @pick_sc).
  @pick_sc — any non-empty Array; predicate reads @is_default per entry and returns @name.

Returns:
  @classes_enrich → new Array in input order; caller input Arrays are NEVER mutated (rhai for
    loop items are copy-on-write values — verified: input map gains no `volumeMode` key).
    Raw-capable drivers yield TWO entries pushed Block-first then Filesystem.
  @get_known_class → Array of 12 `#{driverClass, accessModes, capabilities}` maps; accessModes
    maps hold all four mode keys with boolean values; capabilities key sets vary per driver.
  @get_prefered_sc → the fixed 9-key map `block_readWriteMany`, `block_readWriteOnce`,
    `fs_cheap_readWriteMany`, `fs_fast_readWriteMany`, `fs_readWriteMany`,
    `fs_cheap_readWriteOnce`, `fs_fast_readWriteOnce`, `distibuted_readWriteOnce` (typo frozen —
    consumers @storage_class_selector and ./build_context read it verbatim), `fs_readWriteOnce`;
    each value a class-name @String or the unit `()` left unset.
  @pick_sc → @String `def.name` for the first entry whose @is_default predicate hit, else
    `scs[0].name`. A missing or non-boolean @is_default key reads as unit and simply never
    matches the @find.
  @get_default_access_modes_from_all → `["ReadWriteMany"]` if present in `all`, else
    `["ReadWriteOnce"]` if present, else `all` unchanged (probed: empty in → empty out).

Raises:
  No @throw exists anywhere in this file; the only raises are rhai engine errors escaping its
    own indexing/typelookups:
      - @pick_sc([]) — `Array index 0 out of bounds: array is empty`, annotated
        `@ 'storage_class_enrich'` in the caller frame.
      - @classes_enrich on an entry with no @provisioner key — the key reads as `()` and
        `().contains(...)` aborts `Function not found: contains ((), &str...)`.

Handles:
  Unknown provisioner (no catalog substring hit) → conservative floor: `capabilities` = `#{}`,
    `allAccessModes` = `["ReadWriteOnce"]`, `accessModes` = `["ReadWriteOnce"]`, one
    `Filesystem` entry.
  Missing @capabilities.raw on a matched driver (e.g. `smb`, `nfs`, `filestore`, `efs`,
    `local-path`) — `f.capabilities.raw == true` compares unit to `true` → false → no Block
    twin; only literal `true` expands (probed catalog: `rbd.csi.ceph.com`, `csi.scaleway.com`,
    `ebs.csi.aws.com`, `ebs.csi.eks.amazonaws.com`).
  @get_prefered_sc([]) → full 9-key all-unit map (every bucket guard is a `.len() > 0` check;
    the `pick_sc(many)` fallback in the block branch is never reached with `many` empty when
    `others` is empty because block is then entirely `many`).

Must:
  Match by substring, not equality: catalog @find uses `i.provisioner.contains(k.driverClass)`
    (provisioner CONTAINS catalog driver; `rook-ceph.rbd.csi.ceph.com` matches
    `rbd.csi.ceph.com`, probed), first catalog-array hit wins.
  Every matched entry gets `volumeMode` set to `"Filesystem"` FIRST, then the catalog
    `capabilities` map verbatim, then `allAccessModes` = keys of the catalog accessModes map
    with truthy values in BTreeMap alphabetical order (`ReadOnlyMany`, `ReadWriteMany`,
    `ReadWriteOnce`, `ReadWriteOncePod` order probed).
  Raw twin is a value snapshot BEFORE the Filesystem entry is re-filtered: the Block entry
    keeps `ReadWriteMany` in `allAccessModes` and its `accessModes` derive from that unfiltered
    list (rbd Block → `["ReadWriteMany"]` probed), while the Filesystem twin has
    `ReadWriteMany` removed from both lists (rbd FS → `["ReadWriteOnce"]` probed). Consequence:
    only a raw+RWMany driver's BLOCK twin can ever satisfy the `accessModes ==
    ["ReadWriteMany"]` buckets in @get_prefered_sc.
  @get_prefered_sc buckets: `block*` from `volumeMode=="Block"` split by exact
    `accessModes == ["ReadWriteMany"]`; `fs_readWriteMany` from Filesystem + that exact array;
    FS-single-mode pool = Filesystem whose `accessModes` array-equals exactly
    `["ReadWriteOncePod"]` or `["ReadWriteOnce"]`; when that pool has >1 member,
    `distibuted_readWriteOnce` takes the @pick_sc of NON-`rancher.io/local-path` members and
    `fs_readWriteOnce` the local-path @pick_sc when both kinds exist (probed), single-member
    pools put the same name in both keys.
  Key-name contract: the `accessModes`/`allAccessModes`/`capabilities`/`volumeMode`/
    `provisioner`/`is_default`/`name` keys and all nine preference keys — including the
    `distibuted_readWriteOnce` misspelling — are the frozen interface to
    ./storage_class_selector.rhai and ./build_context.rhai.
  The `fs_cheap_*` / `fs_fast_readWriteMany` / `fs_fast_readWriteOnce` preference slots are
    initialised to `()` and NEVER assigned (no writer exists in 157 lines) — @storage_class_selector
    fast/cheap arms (its lines 5-8, 21-24, 27-30, 45-48) are therefore permanently dead against
    this producer's map (see Tasks).
  The local-path split filter `!s.accessModes.contains(["ReadWriteMany"])` tests a nested
    Array against an array of Strings and is always true — `onlys` always equals the FS pool
    (see Tasks).

Depends on:
  rhai std library only (@find/@filter/@keys/@contains/@push, Array/Map equality, unit-vs-value
    compare) — zero wynil-core registrations are called here (no @k8s_resource, no @throw, no
    JSON/HTTP helpers); cluster data arrives pre-shaped by the caller:
    ./build_context.rhai maps `k8s_resource("StorageClass").list().items` to
    `#{name, provisioner, is_default}` (annotation
    `storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class=="true"`) before calling @classes_enrich.
  ./storage_class_selector.rhai (pending spec) — reads the produced preference key names; the
    misspelled key and the never-set fast/cheap keys are its input shape.
  /agent/tests/rhai_lib.rs — five mock-engine tests (`make_lib_script`, resolver
    `agent/scripts/lib`) cover: field presence on match, unknown floor, raw twin `raw`
    capability, ebs 2-entry expansion + default-over-first via @get_prefered_sc.

Scenario: rbd expands into RWMany Block twin and RWO Filesystem twin
  Given scs = [#{name: "ceph-rbd", provisioner: "rbd.csi.ceph.com", is_default: false}]
  When @classes_enrich runs
  Then len == 2, enriched[0].volumeMode == "Block" with accessModes ["ReadWriteMany"] and
    allAccessModes all four modes, enriched[1].volumeMode == "Filesystem" with accessModes
    ["ReadWriteOnce"] and allAccessModes without ReadWriteMany (all probed)
  And the caller's input map has gained no keys

Scenario: unknown provisioner floor and substring match
  Given provisioner "example.com/mystery"
  Then one Filesystem entry with capabilities `#{}`, allAccessModes and accessModes
    ["ReadWriteOnce"] (probed)
  Given provisioner "rook-ceph.rbd.csi.ceph.com" (unknown verbatim, substring-known)
  Then it matches rbd.csi.ceph.com and gets the full rbd twin treatment (probed)

Scenario: preference map with local-path sharing the FS pool
  Given enriched [cephfs RWMany default-false, mystery RWO default-false,
    rancher.io/local-path RWO default-true]
  When @get_prefered_sc runs
  Then fs_readWriteMany == "cephfs", distibuted_readWriteOnce == "weird" (the non-local-path,
    name-not-default → array-first via @pick_sc), fs_readWriteOnce == the local-path class name
  And block_* and all cheap/fast slots remain () (probed)

Scenario: pick_sc on empty array
  Given scs = []
  When @pick_sc runs
  Then the run aborts `Array index 0 out of bounds: array is empty` — no guard of its own

Tasks:
  [ ] Complete the catalog — source header TODO names the upstream:
      https://storageclass.info/csidrivers/ (csidrivers.yaml).
  [?] The `onlys` filter and the inner `else if onlys.len() > 0` / final `else` branches at
      lines 128-151 are unreachable given `fs_only.len() > 1` and the always-true nested-array
      contains. Decide whether to simplify or leave as future-capable scaffolding.
  [?] `fs_cheap_*`/`fs_fast_readWriteMany`/`fs_fast_readWriteOnce` are never written yet the
      selector reads them. Decide intent: populate (from what signal?) or drop the keys and
      selector arms together.
  [?] The Block twin's accessModes are computed from the UN-filtered allAccessModes, so a raw
      RWMany driver is advertised Block+ReadWriteMany; the Filesystem twin cannot be RWMany.
      Confirm this asymmetry is the design (it is what makes block_readWriteMany fillable)
      rather than an ordering slip on the `b = i` snapshot.
  [?] Keeping `distibuted_readWriteOnce` misspelled is today's frozen cross-file contract;
      decide someday whether it is renamed coordinated with selector/build_context/boxes.
  [ ] Extend /agent/tests/rhai_lib.rs coverage to the unprobed edges: rbd RWMany twin
      asymmetry, local-path preference split, @get_prefered_sc([]) full-unit map, @pick_sc([])
      raise, missing-provisioner raise.

Done when:
  Catalog TODO tracked, the quirk Tasks above have decisions or pinned tests, and the five
    existing + extended @rhai_lib.rs cases are green under `cargo test -p agent`.
